          <section id="shooting-range-and-food" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-5">
            <div class="border-l-4 border-amber-500 pl-4 mb-4">
              <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl lg:text-[26px] font-bold text-slate-900 leading-tight">
                Shooting Range & Refreshment Costs
              </h2>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-4">
              <div class="p-5 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-2xs space-y-2">
                <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Is The Shooting Range Included In The Entrance Fee?</div>
                <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                  <strong>No.</strong> The shooting range is an optional paid activity. It should not be assumed to be included in the basic 135,000 VND international visitor charge. Shooting-range ammunition is charged separately, and current published prices vary by source and weapon. Recent travel sources report roughly 50,000–75,000 VND per round, but this is subject to change. Confirm the current price and minimum purchase requirement at the range. You can also visit Cu Chi without participating in the shooting activity.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="p-5 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-2xs space-y-2">
                <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Are Food And Drinks Included?</div>
                <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                  <strong>No.</strong> Food and drinks are separate from the historical-site admission. Bring water, particularly if visiting during the hotter part of the day. Some visitor experiences also include opportunities to learn about foods associated with life during the historical period (such as a tasting of steamed tapioca with roasted peanut salt and tea), but this should not be interpreted as a complimentary meal included in the entrance fee.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

