              <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl lg:text-[26px] font-bold text-slate-900 leading-tight">
                Can You Visit Cu Chi Tunnels Independently?
              </h2>
            </div>

            <p class="text-slate-700 text-[16px] leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Yes. Independent travel to Cu Chi is possible.</strong> Travelers have reported using:
            </p>

            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-slate-700 text-[15px]">
              <li>Ride-hailing apps (e.g. Grab, Xanh SM)</li>
              <li>Public buses</li>
              <li>Private cars</li>
              <li>Other independent transportation</li>
            </ul>

            <p class="text-slate-700 text-[16px] leading-relaxed">
              Ride-hailing can be convenient for the outbound journey, but availability for the return trip from the rural site can be less predictable. Check the live fare on the app and arrange your return before leaving the site.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-[16px] leading-relaxed">
              Public buses are the lowest-cost option, but they require more time and transfers. Check the current route for your chosen visitor site before departure.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-[16px] leading-relaxed">
              Some independent visitors have also arranged on-site guiding rather than joining a conventional tour. The main advantage is flexibility. The main disadvantage is that you are responsible for getting to the correct site, purchasing admission, managing arrival timing, arranging the return journey, and deciding which optional activities to include. For travelers who want a smooth half-day experience, a private tour removes much of that coordination. See our <a href="/visiting-cu-chi-tunnels-by-private-car" class="text-amber-800 hover:underline font-semibold">Private Car Guide</a>.
